A non-proportion ("non-fill") variant of \code{\link[MiscMetabar:plot_tax_pq]{MiscMetabar::plot_tax_pq()}}:
counts of the chosen taxonomic rank are stacked per sample \strong{without}
being normalised to proportions, so the y-axis reports the raw number
of sequences. Useful when the absolute abundance per sample matters
(e.g. spike-in normalisation, biomass comparisons) and a proportional
view would hide it.

Implemented as a fresh function in \code{ggplotpq} rather than a parameter
on \code{\link[MiscMetabar:plot_tax_pq]{MiscMetabar::plot_tax_pq()}}, so the proportion version keeps its
existing behaviour and the new variant is free to evolve.
}
